WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.480
A couple of days ago, I was invited to a digital
viewing of Elden Ring.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:10.160
It included new screenshots, the opportunity
for Q&amp;A..but most importantly..I got to view

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:16.080
a stunning 16 minute gameplay showcase that..I'm
not allowed to show you for some reason?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:23.130
It's weird, because the showcase was really
well made..so I assume you'll see it soon?

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.369
Until then, you have this video, which will
mainly be audio only

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:32.650
..so hey, while you listen, feel free to tab
out and browse Soul Arts, my art book project,

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.890
now on Kickstarter..

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:38.370
The first thing the player does, is approach
a Grace checkpoint.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:43.610
For those of you who don't know, these are
Elden Ring's version of bonfires..but there's

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.710
more:

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.989
Because the open world is so vast, a gentle
ray of light will shine from the grace, pointing

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:52.449
you towards your next main objective.

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:57.860
To be clear, this doesn't mean your next objective
will be easy - so it might be wise to ignore

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:03.519
the guidance sometimes, and strike out on
your own path, looking for loot.

00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:10.450
At points of lost Grace you can summon the
firekeeper maiden of this game..who I got

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.980
to see in a cutscene.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:19.300
She phases in like a spirit, sits down, and
removes her hood - revealing light strawberry

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:25.380
blonde hair, and olive eyes - one of them
scarred and shut tight.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.970
She introduces herself as "Melina", and offers
you an accord, ending the cutscene.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.480
She's an S-tier maiden character.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.490
You'll see.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:42.860
In my interview it was revealed that you can
level up at Melina, and customise things like

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:47.080
your spirit summons, and equipped weapon skills,
while sitting at the Grace.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.340
Graces also refill this game's equivalent
of an Estus Flask, but since they're are a

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.770
bit harder to come by than Bonfires, you can
also get a bit of health back by defeating

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:01.810
mobs of enemies, which From Software says
should keep you exploring a little bit longer.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:07.500
Beyond Graces, there is another, more traditional
hub location..I'm showing it onscreen now.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.660
Here, NPC's you meet in the outside world
will come to visit you, similar to places

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.230
like Firelink Shrine.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:17.070
In the center is what looks like a Grace checkpoint,
right?

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:22.980
Except it's larger, with threads connected
to weapons lying askew in the middle of the

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.980
table.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:30.320
Perhaps, every time you find a grace in the
outside world, a new thread is added?

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:34.510
Around the table are chairs, presumably where
NPC's will come to sit..

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:43.090
..and the room is very visually distinct from
other hubs we've seen before - It's ornate

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:50.270
and elegant, as befits a Tarnished, a character
who is striving to get this sort of dignity

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.270
back.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.440
I love it.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.080
After leaving the Grace, the character starts
running and summons their mount while moving

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.250
with a smooth, fast animation.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:05.020
It's easy to imagine this being used mid-combat,
whenever you need a burst of speed to get

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.200
away, or close a gap.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.410
Once you see the player actually riding around..you
get a thrill.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:17.410
The previous trailer was great, but it was
cut so often that you couldn't get a sense

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.570
of the vastness of the world.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:26.020
In this video, you get to see the player transition
from exploring that open world into exploring

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:31.990
camps, dungeons, and random encounters around
the place.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:37.880
So, this video, unsurprisingly, reveals a
ton of new information.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:43.780
During the presentation, From Software made
it clear that, generally, you might prefer

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:50.810
to fight on horseback against larger foes
where hit and run tactics are effective, and

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:54.810
dismount to take out multiple enemies more
carefully.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:59.370
Out of combat, you and your horse have a sprint
that doesn't use up your stamina.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.390
This will help you traverse the world.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:05.360
In combat, however, stamina will come back
into play.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:10.950
On horseback, you can easily fire arrows,
fire off sorcery, and of course, swing your

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.950
weapon.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:17.910
I was shown horseback combat in a fight against
this giant wyvern, which starts as a small

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:26.750
speck in the sky, then flies down and obliterates
a mob of hollows standing nearby.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:32.250
From software are calling these Field Bosses,
minibosses varying in difficulty that can

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.710
be fought in the open world.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:39.169
The second field-boss in the trailer is fought
at the end of a co-op showcase, and fights

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:43.840
similarly to those dragonkin in archdragon
peak.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:53.250
When they defeat this field boss, it leaves
a grace checkpoint behind, which I found interesting.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:05:00.870
At some point in the trailer, the player brings
up the map..which has a very hand-drawn style,

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.460
and looks absolutely gorgeous.

00:05:08.671 --> 00:05:15.801
One of the most interesting things I noticed
was an enormous ocean area, with ships and

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:18.432
even what looked like a path demarcated on
it.

00:05:18.432 --> 00:05:26.871
It made me wonder if some sort of ocean exploration
is possible.

00:05:26.871 --> 00:05:30.541
Your location and direction facing are shown
on the map, and From Software mention you

00:05:30.541 --> 00:05:35.911
can set markers to help with exploration - for
example, taking note of a forest that might

00:05:35.911 --> 00:05:43.161
contain crafting ingredients, or places with
a dangerous enemy you haven't yet defeated.

00:05:43.161 --> 00:05:49.201
Marked areas on the map show up as pillars
of light in the distance, helping you move

00:05:49.201 --> 00:05:52.061
towards them.

00:05:52.061 --> 00:06:00.071
You don't fill out your map by exploring,
instead, you collect map fragments that are

00:06:00.071 --> 00:06:01.551
scattered around the world.

00:06:01.551 --> 00:06:09.051
They're clearly trying to build out their
loot tables here, to encourage dungeon diving.

00:06:09.051 --> 00:06:14.021
Finally, once you've discovered a location,
you can easily fast-travel there.

00:06:14.021 --> 00:06:21.041
It's a big step up from Sekiro's world map,
which was pretty useless.

00:06:21.041 --> 00:06:29.161
However, Elden Ring is drawing heavily from
what they learned with Sekiro - adding a jump

00:06:29.161 --> 00:06:35.911
button, and stealth, which play a huge part
in differentiating this game from Dark Souls.

00:06:35.911 --> 00:06:40.401
The next section of the trailer has the player
dismount on a cliff.

00:06:40.401 --> 00:06:45.911
They pull out their binoculars, and scout
out an enemy camp below, planning their assault.

00:06:45.911 --> 00:06:50.522
To complement their stealth, something called
"sleep arrows" have been added, which allow

00:06:50.522 --> 00:06:55.451
you to quietly incapacitate enemies from a
distance, giving you an opportunity to sneak

00:06:55.451 --> 00:06:57.131
past without having to kill them.

00:06:57.131 --> 00:06:58.831
The character does a killing blow on a sleeping
enemy, then attacks another enemy below them

00:06:58.831 --> 00:07:02.601
with a jumping attack, which breaks their
guard and allows for another killing blow.

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:07.591
If that doesn't seem overpowered enough, you
can attack midair, you can shoot your bow

00:07:07.591 --> 00:07:11.221
mid-air..you're basically Sekiro wearing armour.

00:07:11.221 --> 00:07:16.970
Both Sekiro and Dark Souls had combat arts..but
in my opinion, neither Sekiro or Dark Souls

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.731
got weapon arts right.

00:07:18.731 --> 00:07:20.821
However, Elden Ring just might.

00:07:20.821 --> 00:07:26.881
In this game they're called "Skills", and
they're like weapon arts that can be assigned

00:07:26.881 --> 00:07:28.041
to any weapon.

00:07:28.041 --> 00:07:32.991
In this trailer, the character performs wind
blasts from a scimitar, and a thunder strike

00:07:32.991 --> 00:07:34.711
from a polearm.

00:07:34.711 --> 00:07:38.271
I think this will help your character feel
really custom.

00:07:38.271 --> 00:07:44.801
Again, you probably find these hidden around
the world, adding to the loot table in the

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:45.801
game

00:07:45.801 --> 00:07:49.511
Another set of things you can find hidden
around the world are "Spirits of the Deceased",

00:07:49.511 --> 00:07:53.500
items that unlock different sets of NPC's
for summoning.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:58.031
These can only be summoned in difficult areas
that have these obelisks present.

00:07:58.031 --> 00:08:04.051
Some are tanky, some are aggressive, some
are ranged..and some come as a swarm of helpers.

00:08:04.051 --> 00:08:09.201
In one example from the video, the player
summoned a set of like 6 friendly NPC's.

00:08:09.201 --> 00:08:13.571
These phantoms caused chaos, allowing the
player to weave in and out of all the enemies

00:08:13.571 --> 00:08:16.831
they were facing, dealing damage more freely.

00:08:16.831 --> 00:08:21.021
I'd also like to mention..they were wielding
a twinblade in this scene.

00:08:21.021 --> 00:08:24.021
I'm so glad they're bringing this back from
Dark Souls 2.

00:08:24.021 --> 00:08:28.141
According to From Software, spirit summons
use the FP system you'll remember from Dark

00:08:28.141 --> 00:08:30.981
Souls.

00:08:30.981 --> 00:08:34.571
Stronger summons use more FP, and weaker summons
use less.

00:08:34.571 --> 00:08:38.561
This might make it a bit less less overpowered
than I thought at first?

00:08:38.561 --> 00:08:42.560
Since if you summon spirits, you might not
have access to your spells and skills.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:47.711
Still, spirit summons are probably very powerful
by nature, and I anticipate Elden Ring in

00:08:47.711 --> 00:08:54.131
general will be far more accessible to new
players, because of things like this.

00:08:54.131 --> 00:08:59.230
A few sections of the video showcase co-op,
and this is something I'm really excited for,

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:01.610
because it seems less..instanced?

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:02.980
Than in previous games.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:08.121
In the video, two players sneak through the
forest you see in this screenshot, avoiding

00:09:08.121 --> 00:09:12.010
large, terrifying enemies who were patrolling
the area.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:17.480
Later, we delve into an underground dungeon
with our partner, avoiding sen's fortress

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.660
style traps and ambushes together.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:24.881
From Soft have previously mentioned that they
want to reduce the friction required for co-op,

00:09:24.881 --> 00:09:29.710
removing requirements like having humanity
or embers..and I hope they take this all the

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:34.900
way, and make it easy to bring our friends
into our world, and keep them there.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:39.470
I did notice that after defeating a field
boss, the partner didn't seem to disappear.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:45.670
Finally, we make our way to "Stormvale Castle",
the Legacy dungeon of this first open world.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:51.220
If the open world of Elden Ring is Dark Souls
with a horse, then Legacy dungeons are Dark

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.350
Souls with a jump.

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:59.121
From what I saw, they're WAY more vertical
than before, with multiple paths sprawling

00:09:59.121 --> 00:10:03.090
left and right, and layered up and down.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:09.221
Our character talks to an NPC as soon as they
arrive, and the NPC recommends we take the

00:10:09.221 --> 00:10:11.181
back way into the castle.

00:10:11.181 --> 00:10:17.040
The player, however, opts for the main gate
instead..and is instantaneous shot down by

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.220
ballista arrow fire.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:22.371
I'm sure it's possible to roll through this,
but our player quickly changes their mind,

00:10:22.371 --> 00:10:24.371
and takes the back way instead.

00:10:24.371 --> 00:10:30.181
The back way through the castle has more Sekiro
elements - you use jumps to get over rubble,

00:10:30.181 --> 00:10:36.280
avoid guards that signal the alarm, and use
sleep arrows to sneak past giant enemies.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:40.931
Waiting for you at the end is the heavily
armed demigod, whose full intro cinematic

00:10:40.931 --> 00:10:42.711
we get to see.

00:10:42.711 --> 00:10:47.741
One of the cool things I noticed here was
a new sort of counter attack animation that

00:10:47.741 --> 00:10:49.910
can be performed after blocking.

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:52.371
It's this one, from the earlier trailer.

00:10:52.371 --> 00:10:56.650
Basically, when you block an attack in Elden
Ring with a weapon, it seems like you can

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:59.980
quickly follow up with a unique attack animation.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:01.280
I love this idea.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:07.261
In Dark Souls, it was usually always a terrible
idea to block with your weapon, as the stamina

00:11:07.261 --> 00:11:12.191
and chip damage was super high..but now, in
Elden Ring, at least there's an offensive

00:11:12.191 --> 00:11:15.780
benefit to blocking an attack like this.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:21.350
It's not ideal, but it's not as punishing
as it used to be, either.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:26.910
In conclusion, I take back what I said about
it not being big dark souls.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.820
Elden Ring is kind of big Dark Souls.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:32.681
But it's also Sekiro Souls, way more than
I expected, actually.

00:11:32.681 --> 00:11:38.311
It really does seem like the culmination of
everything they've learned up to this point,

00:11:48.051 --> 00:11:53.272
But before I go - would you guys listen to
an audiobook, if I narrated it?

00:11:53.272 --> 00:11:57.522
I'm asking because..soon, you might have the
opportunity to.

00:11:57.522 --> 00:12:03.411
A couple of weeks ago, I revealed our Kickstarter
for "Soul Arts", a premium art book filled

00:12:03.411 --> 00:12:07.821
with the best art from the art competitions
I've been running the last few years.

00:12:07.821 --> 00:12:13.001
It's also a book filled with short stories
on every page..and now, as a reward for all

00:12:13.001 --> 00:12:17.921
the support you guys have given the project,
I'm planning on narrating the entire thing

00:12:17.921 --> 00:12:20.402
for backers to enjoy on YouTube.

00:12:20.402 --> 00:12:25.142
This is a new part of the digital edition
for the book, which almost all backers have

00:12:25.142 --> 00:12:27.431
access to by default.

00:12:27.431 --> 00:13:44.371
So please, enjoy "The Hinterlands", One of
many short stories I'm writing for Soul Arts.

